<title>JAPAN: Fujitsu shares climb to new high for 1997.</title>
<headline>Fujitsu shares climb to new high for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of computer maker Fujitsu Ltd climbed to a new high for this calendar year on Monday morning, helped by recent buying incentives in the high-technology sector sparked by the bullish trend in U.S. computer shares, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0118 GMT, Fujitsu shares were up 20 yen at 1,650, the highest level so far this year. Its volume of 3.124 million shares was the third-heaviest on the Tokyo bourse.</p>
